V = {
"V-prophetic-1":("Who is the rider on the first white horse (Revelation 6:2), and how does he stand to the rider of 19:11, the beast of chapter 13 and the scarlet beast of chapter 17?","The first rider is the Antichrist, the counterfeit of the true rider; the rider of 19:11 is Christ; the beast of chapter 13 is Daniel's little horn; the scarlet beast is the same figure in kingdom form. One person, one career, one end."),
"V-prophetic-2":("Who is the false prophet (the second beast of Revelation 13), what is his work, and how do the dragon, the beast and he work together to their end?","The three form a counterfeit of the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit. The false prophet is a Jewish false prophet rising from the land whose work is to make the world worship the beast; he and the beast are cast alive into the lake of fire."),
"V-prophetic-3":("Who are the woman and the scarlet beast of Revelation 17, what are the seven heads and ten horns, and how does the coalition end?","The beast is the Antichrist in the form of a kingdom and a coalition of kings; the seven heads are seven world kingdoms; the ten horns are ten future rulers. The woman is Mystery Babylon, a religious and commercial world system, destroyed by the beast's coalition."),
"V-prophetic-4":("Where does Daniel's count of seventy weeks begin and end, and what stands between the sixty-ninth week and the seventieth?","Seventy sevens of years from the decree of Artaxerxes to Nehemiah; sixty-nine run to Messiah, who is cut off; the count stops; the prince who shall come confirms the covenant for one week, the future seventieth."),
"V-prophetic-5":("Are the reaping and winepress, Armageddon, the rider of Revelation 19 and the conqueror of Isaiah 63 one judgment, and in what order does it fall?","They are one judgment seen from different sides: the judgment of the nations at Christ's return at the end of Daniel's seventieth week, a campaign and not one clash, ending with the beast and false prophet cast alive into the lake of fire. It is not Gog and Magog."),
"V-covenantal-1":("What did God swear to Abraham, who receives it, and does it stand?","One unconditional covenant of land, nation, name and blessing; its fulfilment belongs to redeemed Israel in the kingdom; the Body is not a party and has Abraham's faith as a pattern only."),
"V-covenantal-2":("Who is Abraham's seed in each use of the word, and who is it not?","The line runs through Isaac and Jacob to Israel and David and comes to its head in Christ; the Body is counted as Abraham's seed only because it belongs to Christ, and is not made Israel or enrolled in Israel's covenants."),
"V-covenantal-3":("What was Abraham's line given to possess, who receives it, and what of the passages that call the Gentile believer an heir?","The land with its borders is Israel's by promise and oath; the Body has its own inheritance in the heavenly places; neither is moved to the other."),
"V-covenantal-4":("Why did God work through two callings, and how do they serve one purpose in Christ?","One eternal purpose in Christ, served by two distinct callings that are never merged: Israel's (promises, land, Kingdom) and the Body's (the Mystery, heavenly places); they meet in one person (Ephesians 1:10)."),
"V-covenantal-5":("What did God swear to David about the throne and the kingdom, and where and when is the throne?","A house, throne and kingdom for ever; the throne is Israel's and earthly, at Jerusalem in the Kingdom; the Body's seat is heavenly and is not called David's throne."),
"V-identity-1":("Who is the bride in prophecy: the wife of the LORD and the wife of the Lamb?","The bride is Israel; the Body of Christ is not the bride; when Paul borrows the marriage pattern he teaches the Body how to love and be faithful without giving it the wife's name."),
"V-identity-2":("Who is the remnant, from Noah and Elijah's seven thousand through the great tribulation?","The remnant is Israel's from first to last; it is not the church or the Body, and not a people the Body replaces, absorbs or joins."),
"V-identity-3":("To whom was the new covenant promised, what did the Cross do to it, and when is it fulfilled?","Promised to the house of Israel and the house of Judah; ratified at the Cross; its fulfilment awaits Israel's restoration; the Body benefits from the blood but is not a party to the covenant."),
"V-identity-4":("Whose is the olive tree of Romans 11, and what share do the Gentiles have in it?","The tree is Israel's; the Gentiles are participants in the root and fatness, not Israel and not natural branches; the tree is not the Body, which is formed by the revelation of the Mystery."),
"V-identity-5":("Whose is the New Jerusalem, and who walks in its light?","The city and community of Israel's prophetic hope, with the twelve tribes' names on its gates; the saved nations walk in its light on the new earth; the Body's destiny is the heavenly places."),
"V-prophecy-mystery-1":("Whose passage is this: Israel's program or the Body's?","Two programs, kept apart by Scripture, ran side by side from Acts 9 to the end of Acts without merging; Acts 28 set Israel's program aside nationally and did not replace it; the Body is not Israel."),
"V-prophecy-mystery-2":("What is the Mystery, what did God reveal in it, to whom, and when?","The Body's program, hid in God, not foretold by the prophets, revealed to Paul beginning in Acts 9, running beside Israel's program through Acts and continuing after."),
"V-prophecy-mystery-3":("What kingdom does Scripture promise, to whom, when was it offered, what became of the offer, and when does it come?","An earthly Davidic kingdom at Jerusalem, offered to Israel and refused, set aside nationally at Acts 28, coming with the King's return for a thousand years; not the church and not the Body's heavenly calling."),
"V-prophecy-mystery-4":("What are the resurrections of Scripture, whose are they, and in what order do they fall?","Christ's is the firstfruits; Israel's is the just at the kingdom and the rest a thousand years later; the Body's is a secret shown to Paul; Ezekiel 37 is a nation's restoration and the Gospel raisings were returns to mortal life."),
"V-prophecy-mystery-5":("Who is judged, where, by whom, and for what?","Separate courts, not one assize: the Cross; the judgment seat of Christ (the Body, no condemnation); Israel in the land; the living nations at the King's return; the beast's kingdom with the thrones; the great white throne for the rest of the dead."),
"V-prophets-1":("By the prophets' own statements, how is a word of the LORD known, what can turn an oracle aside, and what does the LORD swear that cannot be turned?","The prophets give several tests, each for a different question: source, loyalty and fulfilment; announced judgment and blessing are conditional and can be turned, while a sworn word is never turned; read in the wrong order the tests call true prophets false and false prophets true."),
"V-prophets-2":("What does each prophet condemn in Israel's worship, in whose worship, and what does he leave standing?","Each prophet charges the worshipers and the way they worship, names the offerings as the LORD's own appointment, sentences the house and people to judgment and not to abolition, and names the offerings again in his own hope; Hebrews 10 gives the same verdict from the other side, inside Israel's line."),
"V-typology-1":("What did the tabernacle and temple pattern shown in the mount point to in Christ, and where does it not pass to the Body?","The tabernacle is a shadow of heavenly things pointing to Christ; it and the temples belong to Israel's program and are fulfilled in Christ and the Kingdom temple; the Body's temple language is Mystery content, neither fulfilment nor transfer."),
"V-typology-2":("Whose scene is \u201cthe one taken and the other left,\u201d and where does the pattern of separating the judged from the kept end?","The pattern (Noah, Lot, Goshen and the Passover night) separates the judged from the kept before judgment; the Matthew 24 passage is the Tribulation separation in Israel's setting, the one taken in judgment and the one left for the Kingdom, not the Body's gathering."),
"V-typology-3":("How do the priesthoods of Aaron and Melchizedek stand to Christ, and does the Body hold a priesthood?","Christ is a priest after Melchizedek's order, not Aaron's; Melchizedek was a real man; the priesthood of a people is Israel's calling; Paul never calls the Body a priesthood."),
"V-typology-4":("What do the Passover, the Red Sea, the wilderness and the new covenant show as a pattern, and whose is the second exodus?","The named types stand (Passover, the rock, the Lamb); the Exodus, Sinai and the land are Israel's, and so is the promised second exodus; the New Covenant is with Israel and the Body benefits from the blood without being a party."),
}
